{# Responsive HTML reminder (SPEC §6.5).

   Written the way email HTML has to be written, which is not how web HTML is written:

   * Tables for layout. Outlook renders with Microsoft Word's engine, which has no meaningful
     support for flexbox or grid.
   * Inline styles. Gmail strips <style> blocks in several contexts, so anything that matters
     is set on the element.
   * No external resources at all — no images, no web fonts. That is partly SPEC constraint D2,
     and partly that most mail clients block remote content by default, so a design depending on
     an image arrives broken.
   * A max-width of 600px, the long-standing safe width for mobile mail clients.

   CONTENT RULE: nothing clinical, ever. No diagnosis, no condition, no visit reason. A recall
   email travels to an address the practice cannot vouch for, may be read on a shared screen, and
   sits in an inbox indefinitely. "It may be time to schedule your annual visit" is the whole
   message.
#}<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{{ subject }}</title>
  </head>
  <body style="margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#f5f6f8; -webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;">

    {# Preview text: what an inbox shows beside the subject line. Hidden in the body itself.
       Without it, clients show the first visible text, which would be the greeting. #}
    <div style="display:none; max-height:0; overflow:hidden; opacity:0;">
      A friendly reminder from {{ clinic_name }} about your annual visit.
    </div>

    <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
           style="background-color:#f5f6f8; padding:24px 12px;">
      <tr>
        <td align="center">

          <table role="presentation" width="600" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0"
                 style="max-width:600px; width:100%; background-color:#ffffff; border-radius:8px;
                        border:1px solid #e4e6ea; font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,
                        'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;">

            {# Wordmark as text, never an image (SPEC §10) — blocked remote content would
               otherwise leave the email headed by an empty box. #}
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:28px 32px 0 32px;">
                <p style="margin:0; font-size:15px; font-weight:600; color:#1d2939;">
                  {{ clinic_name }}
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>

            <tr>
              <td style="padding:20px 32px 0 32px;">
                <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:16px; line-height:24px; color:#1d2939;">
                  Hi {{ first_name }},
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:16px; line-height:24px; color:#475467;">
                  This is a friendly reminder from {{ clinic_name }} that it may be time to
                  schedule your annual visit.
                </p>
                <p style="margin:0 0 24px 0; font-size:16px; line-height:24px; color:#475467;">
                  {% if clinic_phone %}
                    Please contact our office at
                    <a href="tel:{{ clinic_phone | replace(' ', '') | replace('-', '') }}"
                       style="color:#1f4d8f; text-decoration:none;">{{ clinic_phone }}</a>{% if scheduling_url %}
                    or use the button below{% endif %}.
                  {% elif scheduling_url %}
                    Please use the button below to book a time that suits you.
                  {% else %}
                    Please contact our office to book a time that suits you.
                  {% endif %}
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>

            {% if scheduling_url %}
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:0 32px 8px 32px;">
                {# A table-wrapped button: Outlook ignores padding on an anchor, so the
                   clickable area would collapse to the text without this. #}
                <table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
                  <tr>
                    <td align="center" style="background-color:#1f4d8f; border-radius:6px;">
                      <a href="{{ scheduling_url }}"
                         style="display:inline-block; padding:12px 24px; font-size:15px;
                                font-weight:600; color:#ffffff; text-decoration:none;">
                        Schedule Appointment
                      </a>
                    </td>
                  </tr>
                </table>
              </td>
            </tr>
            {% endif %}

            <tr>
              <td style="padding:24px 32px 0 32px;">
                <hr style="border:none; border-top:1px solid #e4e6ea; margin:0 0 16px 0;" />
                {% if reminder_signature %}
                <p style="margin:0 0 16px 0; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:#475467;
                          white-space:pre-line;">{{ reminder_signature }}</p>
                {% endif %}
                <p style="margin:0; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:#1d2939; font-weight:600;">
                  {{ clinic_name }}
                </p>
                {% if clinic_phone %}
                <p style="margin:0; font-size:14px; line-height:22px; color:#475467;">
                  {{ clinic_phone }}
                </p>
                {% endif %}
                {% if clinic_website %}
                <p style="margin:0 0 4px 0; font-size:14px; line-height:22px;">
                  <a href="{{ clinic_website }}" style="color:#1f4d8f; text-decoration:none;">
                    {{ clinic_website }}
                  </a>
                </p>
                {% endif %}
              </td>
            </tr>

            {# The opt-out. SPEC §6.5 requires it, and every clinic asks about it in the demo. #}
            <tr>
              <td style="padding:20px 32px 28px 32px;">
                {# The anchor is kept on one line on purpose. Breaking it across lines puts a
                   newline inside the element, which HTML renders as a space — so the sentence
                   arrives as "Stop receiving these reminders ." with a gap before the full
                   stop. Small, but it is the kind of detail that makes an email look automated. #}
                <p style="margin:0; font-size:12px; line-height:18px; color:#98a2b3;">
                  You are receiving this because you are a patient of {{ clinic_name }}.
                  <a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}" style="color:#98a2b3; text-decoration:underline;">Stop receiving these reminders</a>.
                </p>
              </td>
            </tr>

          </table>
        </td>
      </tr>
    </table>
  </body>
</html>
